Entries for the New Mexico QSO Party used by in-state (New Mexico) stations
The 33 New Mexico counties (each its own multiplier), the 50 states with DC counted as Maryland, and the 13 Canadian provinces and territories.
DXCC entities other than the USA, Canada, Hawaii and Alaska are the class's DX multiplier, not entries here.
The county file comes FIRST, so a county code wins over any state or province alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md (the rules: District of Columbia counts as Maryland); DC.DOM is NOT included.
NF and LB are read as NL (the last line), as nebraska.dom does; the rules list NL.
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.
https://www.newmexicoqsoparty.org/wp/details/rules/

INCLUDE FILE newmexico_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE S50.DOM
INCLUDE FILE P13.DOM
Nl = NF,LB
